            width='600'
            height='454'
            loading='lazy'
            decoding='async'
            alt='Multilingual touchscreen application designed for the Portorož and Piran tourist information service'
          />

          <figcaption class='case-caption'>
            Multilingual language selection screen for a public tourist-information terminal in
            Portorož
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class='row'>
      <h2 class='case-section-heading'>EKV - Integrated Product Communication</h2>

      <p>
        EKV, short for
        <em>Elektronska knjižica vozila</em>, was an electronic vehicle-logbook system designed to
        record journeys and driver information and help organisations manage fleet use and travel
        costs.
      </p>

      <p>
        I created the visual direction and applied it across packaging, printed communication,
        product labels, software graphics, and technical illustrations. The aim was to make a
        specialised technical system easier to understand and present consistently.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class='row'>
      <div class='case-study-grid'>
        <article class='case-study-block case-study-block--challenge'>
          <h2>A visual system for a technical product</h2>

          <p>
            I developed a recognisable visual language around travel, time, distance, and recorded
            information. Speedometer markings, roads, clocks, maps, and strong red-and-grey blocks
            connected the different materials.
          </p>

          <p>
            The system needed to work across very different dimensions, from product cartons and
            printed sheets to compact software graphics and labels.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>
              EKV wordmark and visual direction
            </li>
            <li>
              Product packaging and carton graphics
            </li>
            <li>
              Smart-card and product-label graphics
            </li>
            <li>
              A consistent visual language across formats
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <figure class='case-study-item case-study-media--explore'>
          <img
            class='thumb'
            src='{{base}}assets/images/design-logina-ekv-packaging-600.webp'
            data-src='design-logina-ekv-packaging-600.webp'
            data-path='assets/images'
            width='600'
            height='420'
            loading='lazy'
            decoding='async'
            alt='EKV product packaging designed for Logina'
          />

          <figcaption class='case-caption'>
            EKV product packaging combining technical information, product illustrations, and the
            wider visual system
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <article class='case-study-block case-study-block--decisions'>
          <h2>Print and sales communication</h2>

          <p>
            The printed materials explained what EKV was, how it worked, and how it could help
            companies reduce administrative errors and manage travel costs more effectively.
          </p>

          <p>
            I organised detailed product information into brochures, information sheets,
            advertisements, technical material, stickers, and other sales-support formats.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>
              Product brochures and information sheets
            </li>
            <li>
              Technical specification material
            </li>
            <li>
              Newspaper advertisements
            </li>
            <li>
              Product stickers and carton labels
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <figure class='case-study-item case-study-media--booking'>
          <img
            class='thumb'
            src='{{base}}assets/images/design-logina-ekv-print-communication-600.webp'
            data-src='design-logina-ekv-print-communication-600.webp'
            data-path='assets/images'
            width='600'
            height='480'
            loading='lazy'
            decoding='async'
            alt='EKV brochure, information sheet, and newspaper advertisement designed for Logina'
          />

          <figcaption class='case-caption'>
            EKV print communication created for product information, advertising, and sales support
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class='row'>
      <div class='case-study-grid'>
        <article class='case-study-block case-study-block--challenge'>
          <h2>Software and technical visuals</h2>

          <p>
            I extended the same visual system into software installation screens, program graphics,
            icons, CD artwork, and other digital assets connected to the product.
          </p>

          <p>
            I also created vector illustrations of the EKV hardware in CorelDRAW. The physical card
            readers themselves were designed by Logina’s technical team; my role was to illustrate
            and present them clearly within the product materials.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>
              Software installation graphics
            </li>
            <li>
              Program and desktop icons
            </li>
            <li>
              Website and presentation visuals
            </li>
            <li>
              Vector illustrations of the existing hardware products
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <figure class='case-study-item case-study-media--explore'>
          <img
            class='thumb'
            src='{{base}}assets/images/design-logina-ekv-digital-design-600.webp'
